    17	# Publishing one arm is serialised by an `flock` on a per-arm lock FILE. The lock is held
    18	# by a holder process leased to this launcher's life, never on a descriptor of the
    19	# launcher's own: **it vanishes within ~1 s of the launcher's exit or death and is never
    20	# inherited by the trainer or the log sink**. There is no cleanup code, no owner record
    21	# and no stale-lock concept -- nothing to clear by hand and nothing to get wrong (plan
    22	# section 11 amendment A1, close review 6).
