   892	    # pid of the arm answered a liveness probe, the attempt has no completion receipt and
   893	    # is not the published `final`, and its marker was older than the grace. A trainer
   894	    # that never registered cannot be seen at all -- which is why the tombstone above is
   895	    # written first and never removed (close review 11 and 12, wording).
   896	    say "RESOLVED $attempt: marker older than ${UNRESOLVED_GRACE_S}s, no recorded pid of" \
   897	        "this arm alive, no completion receipt, not the published final. It can never be" \
   898	        "published, and the tombstone refuses any trainer of it that is still to come"
