CommitDate: Mon Sep 28 05:18:33 2026 -0400

    exp11 fix18 (GREEN): the launcher asks identity questions, and carries no paths
    
    probe_path yields only a validated mode; probe_link only says whether a link is there;
    and every guard that used to compare a returned path now asks `same_path` or
    `same_parent` -- `publishes` (final and this attempt are one file), already_published,
    check_final_conflict, abort_recovery, the resolution's published check, the scan's
    exclusion of its target, and check_attempt's containment, which also checks the
    attempt_<UTC> name on the slash-stripped basename. The REPLACING line prints `readlink`
    for the operator and no decision reads it. The health check gained the identity question
    (a file against itself, and against another). The crafted-verdict regressions are now
    malformed answers -- a missing mode, an extra field, another protocol's word -- since a
    forged path cannot be expressed at all, and two spelling regressions show `//`, `/./`
    and a trailing slash resolving and publishing normally.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

